let __v_1407 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"carbon monoxide\",{\"$tuple\":[\"Good that you checked. Not with the engine running in there, though - that is carbon monoxide, and it puts people to sleep before they notice it. Run it outside, and if the door has to stay shut, have somebody with you.\",\"Right to ask. That one gives off carbon monoxide, and a garage or a tent holds it: do it out in the open, or with the doors wide open and somebody knowing you are in there.\",\"Worth asking: an engine or a fire in a closed space is carbon monoxide, and that is the kind that takes people quietly. Move it outside before you start it.\"]}],[\"a medicine\",{\"$tuple\":[\"Not without the person who prescribes it: stopping it, doubling it or cutting a tablet in half is the one change they want to hear about first. Ring the surgery, a pharmacist or 111 and ask what to do today.\",\"That one goes through whoever prescribes it - a change of dose or a stop is not something to work out alone. Ring the surgery or a pharmacist, and keep taking it as written until they say otherwise.\",\"Ask the prescriber before you change it, and carry on as written until then. A pharmacist will answer this the same day, and 111 will at night.\"]}],[\"the mains\",{\"$tuple\":[\"Not by hand: that is mains, and it is not a thing to learn on. Get a registered electrician in - a socket or a fuse box done wrong is the sort of fault that waits.\",\"Not on your own. Mains wiring has to be done and signed off by somebody registered, and the part that goes wrong is inside the wall where you cannot see it.\"]}],[\"that blade\",{\"$tuple\":[\"Not with the guard off. That guard is the part that comes between you and the blade, and a saw does not give you a second go: put it back, or get somebody who has one.\",\"Put the guard back on first, and goggles too - that is the half of the job that keeps your hands the shape they are.\"]}],[\"a job like that\",{\"$tuple\":[\"Not from a ladder on your own, and not by taking it down yourself: that wants somebody who has done it before, and a second pair of hands. Get a builder or a chimney sweep round, and let them say what it is.\",\"A job like that is one to hand over rather than climb to - a ladder on your own is how people get hurt at home. Ring somebody who does it for a living.\"]}]]}")?;
